{"availability":"available","full":"GeiserX/VPN-Bypass","name":"VPN-Bypass","description":"macOS menu-bar app for fine-grained VPN routing: bypass the VPN for chosen domains/services, force others through it, or (Custom mode) route each domain/subnet out a specific egress — direct, a specific VPN, an HTTP/SOCKS5 proxy, or a Tailscale peer. Includes a vpnb CLI.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Swift","stars":126,"forks":11,"created":"2026-01-14T17:37:03Z","updated":"2026-10-08T10:21:32Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://geiserx.github.io/VPN-Bypass/","topics":["cisco","corporate-vpn","dns","globalprotect","homebrew","macos","macos-app","macos-menubar","menu-bar-app","network-tools","networking","privacy","routing","security","socks5","split-tunneling","swiftui","tailscale","vpn","vpn-bypass"],"demo":"https://geiserx.github.io/VPN-Bypass/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.097Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.097Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.097Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:21.589Z","stars":126,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.097Z","stars":126,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A macOS menu bar app that decides which traffic goes through your VPN. Pick the services and domains that should skip it, or the few that must use it, and it keeps the routes right as the VPN reconnects and addresses change.","Corporate VPN clients send everything through the tunnel, so streaming stalls, AirPlay and Chromecast break, and personal traffic crosses the company network. Most clients lock their own split tunnelling, and a route added by hand is gone at the next reconnect or when a CDN moves. VPN Bypass adds the routes for you from a menu bar dropdown and puts them back every time the VPN or the network changes.","The dropdown in Bypass mode, and the Settings window on the Services tab"],"features":["Three modes: Bypass sends the destinations you list around the VPN, VPN Only sends only them through it, and Custom routes each rule where you say, first match wins.","37 built-in service packs (Telegram, WhatsApp, YouTube, Netflix, Spotify, Zoom, GitHub and more) plus any domain, wildcard or subnet you add.","In Custom mode a rule can exit direct, through a specific VPN when several are up, through an HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy, or through a Tailscale peer.","Routes come back on their own when the VPN reconnects or the network changes, and domains are re-resolved as their addresses rotate.","Detects GlobalProtect, Cisco AnyConnect, OpenVPN, WireGuard, FortiClient, Zscaler, Cloudflare WARP, Pulse Secure, Check Point and Tailscale exit nodes."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GeiserX/VPN-Bypass/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ee961fc3e30a50bed96b8af0351ac7035bb41180c7c74b104e643e419ddf0838","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:21.720Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.224Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A macOS menu bar app that decides which traffic goes through your VPN. Pick the services and domains that should skip it, or the few that must use it, and it keeps the routes right as the VPN reconnects and addresses change.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GeiserX/VPN-Bypass/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"Optional /etc/hosts DNS bypass, route verification, notifications, launch at login, and config import and export.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GeiserX/VPN-Bypass/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"ee961fc3e30a50bed96b8af0351ac7035bb41180c7c74b104e643e419ddf0838","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GeiserX/VPN-Bypass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.224Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T10:21:32Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GeiserX/VPN-Bypass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.225Z","hash":"ee961fc3e30a50bed96b8a